The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
alg = __crypto_alg_lookup(name, type | test, mask | test);
if (!alg && test)
    alg = __crypto_alg_lookup(name, type, mask) ? ERR_PTR(-ELIBBAD) : NULL;
```
Reason:
The first statement attempts to look up an algorithm with the tested flag set, and if it fails, the second statement incorrectly assumes that the absence of an algorithm indicates a failure, returning `-ELIBBAD` even if the algorithm is in a "larval" state, which should not be treated as a failure.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (alg && !crypto_is_larval(alg)) {
    crypto_mod_put(alg);
    alg = ERR_PTR(-ELIBBAD);
}
```
Reason:
These statements check if the algorithm is not in a "larval" state before returning `-ELIBBAD`. This ensures that only non-larval algorithms are treated as failures, thus preventing the erroneous error code when the algorithm is still being initialized.

